00:30:13.910 --> 00:30:17.757
If we come back in a year's
time, we'll have Tim on.

00:30:17.757 --> 00:30:18.840
We'll see if you're right.

00:30:18.840 --> 00:30:19.280
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Deal.

00:30:19.280 --> 00:30:20.120
MARK MANDEL: Deal.

00:30:20.120 --> 00:30:22.520
Awesome, well, Tim, thank you so
much for spending time with us.

00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:23.510
We really appreciate it.

00:30:23.510 --> 00:30:25.718
This has been a great
conversation around Kubernetes.

00:30:25.718 --> 00:30:27.917
And thank you so much for
helping start the project.

00:30:27.917 --> 00:30:29.000
I mean, I love Kubernetes.

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:29.840
It's one of my favorite things.

00:30:29.840 --> 00:30:30.140
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:30:30.140 --> 00:30:30.710
Thank you so much.

00:30:30.710 --> 00:30:31.330
TIM HOCKIN: No, thank--

00:30:31.330 --> 00:30:32.370
MARK MANDEL: Thank you
so much for joining us.

00:30:32.370 --> 00:30:33.140
TIM HOCKIN: Thank you
guys for having me.

00:30:33.760 --> 00:30:35.780
MARK MANDEL: Thanks again
to Tim for joining us

00:30:35.780 --> 00:30:37.130
for today's interview.

00:30:37.130 --> 00:30:39.440
As we've said a couple
